   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Question words in Spanish",
     "texto": [
      "In Spanish, question words carry a written accent mark in both direct and indirect questions: **qué**, **quién**, **cómo**, **dónde**, **cuándo**, **cuánto**, **cuál**, and **por qué**.\n\nIn questions with an explicit subject, the verb normally precedes the subject:\n- *¿Dónde vive Ana?*\n- *¿Cuándo es la clase?*\n\nNote the difference between question and reason:\n- **¿Por qué?** (two words, accented) asks why.\n- **Porque** (one word, unaccented) means because in the explanation."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Word order in questions",
     "texto": [
      "When asking questions with a question word and an explicit subject, the standard order is: question word + verb + subject.\n\nWe use **cuál** with the verb **ser** to ask for specific identity details, phone numbers, or addresses."
     ],
